---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal title="Privacy policy | Bridge" description="How Bridge collects, uses and protects information. Bridge serves Lincoln and Omaha, Nebraska." heading="Privacy policy">

        <p class="mt-3 text-base">Effective date: <strong>October 12, 2026</strong></p>

        <div class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-line bg-green-tint p-5">
          <p><strong>Plain-English summary:</strong> We collect only the information needed to coordinate and deliver non-medical appointment support. This includes logistics, mobility notes, and updates for your trusted contact. <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong></p>
        </div>

        <h2>1) Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Bridge collects, uses, and shares information when you visit our
          website or request/receive services.
        </p>

        <h2>2) Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact info:</strong> Name, phone number, and email.</li>
          <li><strong>Appointment details:</strong> Pickup/drop-off addresses, appointment location, and timing.</li>
          <li><strong>Mobility &amp; safety:</strong> Notes on walker/wheelchair use, stairs, or access instructions.</li>
          <li><strong>Trusted contact:</strong> Information for the person authorized to receive the Completion Report.</li>
          <li><strong>Service notes:</strong> The Bridge Completion Report and logs related to service delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Communications:</strong> Messages and emails related to scheduling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3) Health information (important)</h2>
        <p>
          Bridge is a <strong>non-medical service</strong>. Please do not send unnecessary medical details.
          If limited health-related context is shared, such as mobility needs or simple logistics, Bridge uses it only to coordinate safe appointment support.
          We treat sensitive information with care and minimize data retention for any health-related notes.
        </p>

        <h2>4) How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Coordinate and deliver services (booking, matching, routing, timing)</li>
          <li>Safety planning (mobility notes, access instructions)</li>
          <li>Customer support and issue resolution</li>
          <li>Send confirmations and updates you request</li>
          <li>Improve the service and website performance</li>
          <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, or unsafe behavior</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5) How we share information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>With the Bridge Captain</strong> assigned to your service (logistics, mobility notes, and contact info).</li>
          <li><strong>With the Trusted Contact</strong> only when authorized to receive the Completion Report.</li>
          <li><strong>With service providers</strong> that help us operate (e.g., payment processors, booking forms).</li>
          <li><strong>Our forms are run by Tally</strong> (tally.so). When you send a request or an application, Tally stores what you submit on its servers in the European Union, and emails a copy to us.</li>
          <li><strong>For legal/safety reasons</strong> (to comply with law or respond to an emergency/911 situation).</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong></p>

        <h2>6) Cookies &amp; analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Plausible Analytics to count visits and a few actions on the site (for example, form submissions,
          taps on our phone number and file downloads), and to see which link or flyer brought a visitor here.
          Plausible doesn't use cookies, doesn't collect personal information, and doesn't track you across other sites.
          If you arrive through a link with a source tag (for example <code>?src=clinic</code>), that tag is saved with
          any request you send so we know how you found us.
        </p>

        <h2>7) Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep information as long as necessary to provide services, comply with legal requirements, and
          resolve disputes. We aim to retain only what we need.
        </p>

        <h2>8) Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards. No system is 100% secure, but we
          work to reduce risk and limit data collection.
        </p>

        <h2>9) Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Request access, correction, or deletion of your personal information where applicable</li>
          <li>Opt out of non-essential communications</li>
          <li>Control cookies through your browser</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10) Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Bridge services are not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children
          under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>11) Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy. The "Effective date" above reflects the latest version.
        </p>

        <h2>12) Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Call or text <a href="tel:+18159950115" data-track-loc="privacy">815-995-0115</a>, or use our <a href="/book">request form</a>.
        </p>

        <hr class="my-10 border-line" />
        <p>
          Also see: <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        </p>
</Legal>
